{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1167360-running-wod-games-on-roll20","id":1167360,"title":"Running WoD Games On roll20?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-13T11:10:47-08:00","id":1167360,"title":"Running WoD Games On roll20?","content":"Has anyone done this (And might be willing to give some pointers?)<br /> <br /> I get the basic mechanics of how roll20 works, but I'm having a lot of trouble finding appropriate tile sets, backgrounds and maps, since most of the material on the service is geared towards DnD/Pathfinder","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/nbylxup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n77xu8p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1667-novagain","name":"Novagain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T16:33:42-08:00","id":1167444,"title":"","content":"Try looking for the modern tile sets and backgrounds. I haven't run a WoD game using roll20, but I found some cyberpunk sets and zombie sets worked nicely for Corporia, which is a 'chaos and the Arthurian knights come back to a corporate dystopia' setting.<br /> <br /> Also, you can use your journal to hold photos, maps, and even documents. So, if you have found other material, you can import some of it into Roll20. Tokentool and other token creation software can help you make tokens.<br /> <br /> I rarely GM on Roll20 and I've played sporadically since my group left Maptool for Roll20, but the program will do a lot of work for you if you put in the time to learn it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T09:06:42-08:00","id":1167668,"title":"","content":"I honestly just use google hangouts","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>For different game play videos of White Wolf Games from my play group<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBUyj7h-xIhwsM3kHK56SRA\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBU...IhwsM3kHK56SRA</a><br /> <a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night\" target=\"_blank\">https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night</a><br /> If you want to find White Wolf game play media or subject matter media<br /> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11618-christopherzacher","name":"ChristopherZacher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11618_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"631"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T12:18:15-08:00","id":1167737,"title":"","content":"Personally, when i use Roll20 (which is every game now that I am where I am) for WoD and CofD games here's what I do:<br /> <br /> 1. Use a map of the location / city / state / town / etc. <br /> 2. I use a image depicting the scene. If it's in a warehouse, I use a warehouse with the creepy overtones I need. I add to the background with things like NPC character art if needed. I then also reveal the clues of the scene or whatever gets revealed by using the GM layer and revealing them on the Token layer...this can be literally anything from a new NPC popping in to the scene, a letter, clue, or what have you. <br /> 3. Music and sound effects. These create a certain atmosphere and in my opinion are very important in particular to these types of games. Sound effects are great because they can be triggered whenever needed as well.<br /> <br /> The only time I use maps is in combat in which it depends on where they are. In a Geist game I am running, I have a mausoleum map I did using Campaign Cartographer 3 and creating the map from scratch. I layered that on top of a background art like above scenes and also had music/sfx playing to bring a certain atmosphere. Don't forget to also have a player page. This includes each player's art, their character info (just basic important information) and also any notes from last sessions including conditions/experience/etc.<br /> <br /> Hope this helps even a bit. Personally I've had a lot of success in these games over on Roll20 so it would be awesome to see more WoD / CofD played on there!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Kinda I want to&quot; - Trent Reznor<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent.ftpa1-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/27973518_2040009129348529_5319855605701568493_n.jpg?oh=9c85c5c9d4a0769a1249ea2f3e62ca43&amp;oe=5B002AA5\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":""